lar buildings, industrial plant and more. The transport itself is often the shortest part of the job. Most of the work happens before anything is lifted.\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch2\u003eStart with accurate data\u003c/h2\u003e\u003cp\u003eEverything depends on precise dimensions, weights and centres of gravity. Drawings from the manufacturer are the starting point, and they should be confirmed against the finished item before transport plans are locked in.\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch2\u003eRoute surveys\u003c/h2\u003e\u003cp\u003eFor road legs, a route survey checks bridge limits, overhead clearances, turning circles and road surfaces between pickup and delivery. It shows where powerlines may need to be lifted, signs removed or traffic managed, and how long each of those steps will take.\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch2\u003ePermits and escorts\u003c/h2\u003e\u003cp\u003eOversize and overmass loads need permits from road authorities, and many also need pilot vehicles or police escorts. Approval times vary between states and authorities, so applications should be lodged early in the planning process.\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch2\u003eEngineered loading\u003c/h2\u003e\u003cp\u003eLift plans, lashing calculations and stowage plans make sure the cargo is secured for the forces it will face on the road, at sea or in the air. Specialist equipment such as heavy lift cranes, self-propelled modular transporters or flat rack containers is booked to match.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eInvolve your logistics partner while the equipment is still being built.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eAllow time for permit approvals in your project schedule.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eAgree on site access and offloading arrangements before the cargo ships.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e","cover_image":null,"cover_image_alt":null},"related":[{"id":"31322c61-0215-48c4-815b-d621b1d8e694","slug":"fcl-or-lcl-choosing-the-right-ocean-freight-option","title":"FCL or LCL? Choosing the right ocean freight option","category":"Ocean Freight","excerpt":"Full container or shared space? A practical look at cost, transit time and risk so you can book the right ocean service for every shipment.","published_at":"2026-09-29"},{"id":"4bf8b293-4f72-41f6-b760-57ba1cacd285","slug":"what-a-licensed-customs-broker-does-for-importers","title":"What a licensed customs broker actually does for importers","category":"Customs","excerpt":"Classification, valuation, duty and biosecurity all have to line up before goods are released. Here is what a broker handles on your behalf.","published_at":"2026-09-22"},{"id":"c74ac840-3798-4008-882c-478b5bca6df2","slug":"choosing-an-air-freight-service-level","title":"Express, priority or economy: picking an air freight service level","category":"Air Freight","excerpt":"Air freight is not one product. Matching the service level to the urgency of your cargo can save money without putting deadlines at risk.","published_at":"2026-09-15"}],"news":[{"id":"31322c61-0215-48c4-815b-d621b1d8e694","slug":"fcl-or-lcl-choosing-the-right-ocean-freight-option","title":"FCL or LCL? Choosing the right ocean freight option"},{"id":"4bf8b293-4f72-41f6-b760-57ba1cacd285","slug":"what-a-licensed-customs-broker-does-for-importers","title":"What a licensed customs broker actually does for importers"},{"id":"c74ac840-3798-4008-882c-478b5bca6df2","slug":"choosing-an-air-freight-service-level","title":"Express, priority or economy: picking an air freight service level"}]},"__N_SSG":true},"page":"/insights/[slug]","query":{"slug":"planning-project-cargo-permits-surveys-and-load-engineering"},"buildId":"zlvk7yHoyxO_6eey2QNrr","isFallback":false,"isExperimentalCompile":false,"gsp":true,"scriptLoader":[]}</script><style is:global>[data-modulify-badge]{transition:transform .18s ease,filter .18s ease;will-change:transform}[data-modulify-badge]:hover{transform:translateY(-2px);filter:drop-shadow(0 6px 16px rgba(0,0,0,.16))}[data-modulify-badge]:active{transform:translateY(0)}</style><style is:glob